    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite) play four deals anticlockwise. Each deal: dealer gives 15 cards to the player to his right, 15 to partner, 15 to the player to his left, and 17 to himself; dealer then discards two cards face-down (scarto). Player to dealer's right leads to the first trick. Follow suit if possible; if not, play a trump if possible; otherwise play any card. Trick with trumps is won by highest trump; trick without trumps by highest card of led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next. The Fool may be played to any trick and never wins; it is added to the team of whoever played it. Team with more than 57 of the 114 points over the four deals wins the game.",
    Player: "Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite) play four deals anticlockwise. Each deal: dealer gives 15 cards to the player to his right, 15 to partner, 15 to the player to his left, and 17 to himself; dealer then discards two cards face-down (scarto). Player to dealer's right leads to the first trick. Follow suit if possible; if not, play a trump if possible; otherwise play any card. Trick with trumps is won by highest trump; trick without trumps by highest card of led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next. The Fool may be played to any trick and never wins; it is added to the team of whoever played it. Team with more than 57 of the 114 points over the four deals wins the game.",
    objective: 'Score 57 or more points from a pool of 114 available points.',
    gameplay: "Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite) play four deals anticlockwise. Each deal: dealer gives 15 cards to the player to his right, 15 to partner, 15 to the player to his left, and 17 to himself; dealer then discards two cards face-down (scarto). Player to dealer's right leads to the first trick. Follow suit if possible; if not, play a trump if possible; otherwise play any card. Trick with trumps is won by highest trump; trick without trumps by highest card of led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next. The Fool may be played to any trick and never wins; it is added to the team of whoever played it. Team with more than 57 of the 114 points over the four deals wins the game.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit if possible; if void in suit led, must play a trump if possible.',
      'Fool may be played to any trick; it never wins and is not captured; it counts for the team of the player who played it.',
      'Dealer may not discard 5-point cards (Kings, Trump 21, Trump 1, Fool).',
      '57 or more points of 114 wins a deal; team ahead on total points after four deals wins the game.',
      'Partners may communicate about their cards and tactics within defined limits (open communication).',
    ],
